  "name": "Holding Pattern",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "description": "The gatekeepers need more time to read the mine signals. Stretch each one-tick pulse into ten ticks of the same sign, then return to zero. Pulses are at least ten ticks apart; a new pulse may arrive exactly when the previous hold ends. A fixed processing delay is allowed. The checker starts at your first nonzero output and then checks every tick, including silence.",
